  "about": "Format version 12's addition (log-format §6), following v11.json's position 30. Position 31: a `declared` function `loan_days` that carries `with_the_set`: another declaration of the same set follows in its append, and the records the set computes again are computed once, at its last declaration (§2.3). The vector holds the line, not the set's last declaration, so it is a vector of lines and not a log a fold accepts: a log that ends inside a set is damaged, and its fold is refused (§2.3). `negatives` holds the line written as version 11, its hash made right: a reader refuses it, since version 12 added what it carries. Position 32: a `value_type_migrated` that renames `lent` to `out` in the records of `loan` (§2.2). Position 33: a `write_proposed` of a `migrate_value_type` that carries `renames`, with its report's `renamed` counts (Appendix A). `negatives` holds each written as version 11 too.",
